  "result": "Default `[]` is built once, when `def` runs, not per call. Every call that omits `items` gets that same list object, so `append` mutates it. `add(1)` adds 1, then `add(2)` appends 2 to that same list: `[1, 2]`.\n\nFix: use `None` as sentinel, create new list per call.\n\n```python\ndef add(x, items=None):\n    if items is None:\n        items = []\n    items.append(x)\n    return items\n```\n\nNow `add(1)` returns `[1]`, `add(2)` returns `[2]`.",
